From b563e6038143ccfcfae2660fccba21285309202e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaming Zhang <772577952@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:29:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pkg, syz-manager, vm: add adaptive snapshot restoration with
 random selection

Migrate snapshot restoration and adaptive restart mechanism into syzkaller
with random snapshot bank selection on soft reboot.

The adaptive controller supports four actions:
- Continue fuzzing in-place
- Save checkpoint snapshot
- Soft reboot by restoring a randomly chosen snapshot from the snapshot bank
- Hard reboot by restarting the VM instance

Features:
- pkg/adaptive: controller, linear UCB bandit learner, snapshot bank with
  random snapshot selection, lineage recovery, and concurrency limits
- pkg/tsc: TSC timer and TSC frequency calibration on x86_64
- pkg/corpus: return bool on Save to detect new seeds
- pkg/fuzzer: VMFeedback collection and queue executor validity
- pkg/mgrconfig: crash_snapshot and adaptive_restart config options
- syz-manager: snapshot lifecycle management, lease control, and stats
- vm/qemu: QMP savevm, loadvm, and delvm commands with TSC pinning
